<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Hebrew copy. Android picks this when the device language is Hebrew; every
  other language falls back to the English default in values/.

  The qualifier is "iw", not "he": Android's resource resolver still uses the
  legacy ISO code for Hebrew. It looks wrong and is correct.

  Voice: spoken Hebrew, plural second person (אתם), never translated-sounding.
  Position: willpower does not work, and עצור does not ask for any. The copy and
  the mechanism have to back each other up, so nothing here may promise behavior
  the app does not actually implement.
  Never use em-dashes. Regular hyphens only.
-->
